<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original; own earlier source/glossary preparation is disclosed and no English-first proposal or semantic finding was read. The first outer world is banked once; the second outer world and the fourth world are English reprises. The three Tibetan grub predicates are not indiscriminately mapped to created: only the third, in the human-karma clause, owns created. Earlier predicate relations, collected and the expanded liquid referents remain unwrapped rather than falsely nulled. First mi'i owns singular human as karma owner; second owns plural humans as world occupants. Dvangs/sweet is a contextual source attestation, explicitly differing from the glossary's liquid equivalent; the full physical C05 reading and matching source pairs preserve it, and no new glossary definition or source correction is asserted. Shing is represented through punctuation; the remaining causal and anaphoric frames are distributed. Sogs owns the full closing gesture. No new erratum is established from these digital matches; C16:844's appended following heading is a registered apparatus class, not part of this C05 source.</div>
